<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's real end up 0.14 pct in commercial market.</title>
<headline>Brazil's real end up 0.14 pct in commercial market.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's real rose 0.14 percent to close at 1.0764 per dollar in the commercial foreign exchange market in calm trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the interbank floating rate market, the local currency closed off 0.01 percent at 1.0801 per dollar, while in the parallel market it closed flat at 1.138 against the greenback. they added.</p>
<p>((--Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
